      'acceptedAnswer': {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        'text': 'Under the Inflation Reduction Act, Part D prescription drug out-of-pocket costs are capped at a strict maximum of $2,100 per year in 2026. Once you pay $2,100 in covered drug costs, you pay $0 for the rest of the calendar year.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      'name': 'What is the out-of-pocket maximum for Medicare Advantage in 2026?',
      'acceptedAnswer': {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        'text': 'For 2026, CMS mandates that in-network Maximum Out-of-Pocket (MOOP) limits for Medicare Advantage plans cannot exceed $9,250. For combined in-network and out-of-network services on PPO plans, the maximum limit is $13,900.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      'name': 'How is IRMAA calculated and how do I know if I owe it?',
      'acceptedAnswer': {
        '@type': 'Answer',
