    <p class="pillar-meta">
      Last reviewed by the Seniors Audit research team on
      <time datetime={lastUpdated}>{displayDate}</time>
      <span class="pillar-meta-sep">·</span>
      By <a href="/about/emmanuel-tuyishimire/" style="color: inherit; text-decoration: underline;">Emmanuel Tuyishimire</a>
      <span class="pillar-meta-sep">·</span>
      <span>~24 min read</span>
    </p>

    <h1 class="pillar-h1">Medicare Costs 2026: The Complete Financial Guide &amp; Calculator Hub</h1>

    <!-- AEO Direct Answer Block -->
    <aside class="aeo-direct-answer" aria-label="Quick Answer" id="quick-answer">
      <p class="aeo-label">Quick Answer</p>
      <p class="aeo-text">
        In 2026, standard Medicare costs include a $0 premium for Part A (for those with 40+ work credits) with a $1,736 deductible per hospital benefit period, and a $202.90 monthly premium for Part B with a $283 annual deductible. Part B charges a 20% coinsurance with no annual cap under Original Medicare. Part D prescription drug out-of-pocket costs are capped at $2,100 per year, while Medicare Advantage plans have an in-network maximum out-of-pocket ceiling of $9,250.
      </p>
    </aside>

    <!-- Lead Paragraph -->
    <p class="article-introduction">
      Estimating what you will actually spend on Medicare requires looking beyond advertised $0-premium plans. Medicare costs consist of monthly premiums, annual deductibles, copayments, coinsurance percentages, and income-based adjustments like IRMAA. We compiled this guide, verified against official figures from the <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/medicare-and-you" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CMS Medicare and You 2026 handbook</a> and the <a href="https://www.cms.gov/newsroom/fact-sheets/2026-medicare-parts-b-premiums-deductibles" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CMS 2026 Premiums &amp; Deductibles Fact Sheet</a>, to give you total cost clarity and direct access to our suite of calculation tools.
    </p>

    <!-- Interactive Decision Doors / Quick Navigation -->
    <div class="decision-intent-banner">
      <p class="decision-intent-heading">What would you like to calculate today?</p>
      <div class="decision-intent-grid">
        <a href="#part-b-costs" class="decision-pill">
          <span class="pill-icon">📊</span>
          <span class="pill-text"><strong>Part B Premiums</strong>Standard &amp; IRMAA</span>
        </a>
        <a href="#part-a-costs" class="decision-pill">
          <span class="pill-icon">🏥</span>
          <span class="pill-text"><strong>Hospital Costs</strong>Part A Deductibles &amp; Coinsurance</span>
        </a>
        <a href="#part-d-costs" class="decision-pill">
          <span class="pill-icon">💊</span>
          <span class="pill-text"><strong>Prescription Cap</strong>$2,100 Part D Out-of-Pocket Cap</span>
        </a>
        <a href="#irmaa-tiers" class="decision-pill">
          <span class="pill-icon">📈</span>
          <span class="pill-text"><strong>IRMAA Surcharges</strong>Income Brackets &amp; Appeals</span>
        </a>
        <a href="#assistance-programs" class="decision-pill">
          <span class="pill-icon">🤝</span>
          <span class="pill-text"><strong>Financial Assistance</strong>MSPs &amp; Extra Help</span>
        </a>
        <a href="#all-calculators" class="decision-pill">
          <span class="pill-icon">🧮</span>
          <span class="pill-text"><strong>Interactive Calculators</strong>All 8 Free Medicare Tools</span>
        </a>
      </div>
